----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party data

The files under data/brenda/ are derived from BRENDA, release 2023.1
(https://www.brenda-enzymes.org), and are redistributed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

  Chang A, Jeske L, Ulbrich S, Hofmann J, Koblitz J, Schomburg I, Neumann-
  Schaal M, Jahn D, Schomburg D. BRENDA, the ELIXIR core data resource in
  2021: new developments and updates. Nucleic Acids Research 49:D498-D508.

Formation energies are from eQuilibrator (component contribution) at pH 7.4,
ionic strength 0.25 mol/L, pMg 3.0 and 298.15 K. Reaction structure and
stoichiometry are from the Yeast9 reconstruction of Saccharomyces cerevisiae.

The file data/yeast-GEM.xml is release 9.0.2 of yeast-GEM, the Yeast9 reconstruction
(https://github.com/SysBioChalmers/yeast-GEM), redistributed unchanged under
CC BY 4.0.

  Zhang C, Sanchez BJ, Li F, Eiden CWQ, Scott WT, Liebal UW, Blank LM, Mengers HG,
  Anton M, Rangel AT, Mendoza SN, Zhang L, Nielsen J, Lu H, Kerkhoven EJ. Yeast9:
  a consensus genome-scale metabolic model for S. cerevisiae curated by the
  community. Molecular Systems Biology 20(10) (2024). doi:10.1038/s44320-024-00060-7

The files data/external/ecoli_invivo_kapp.csv and
data/external/ecoli_invivo_concentrations.csv hold numbers derived from two
repositories released under the MIT licence, whose copyright notices follow.
Both are distributed under the same permission notice as this repository,
given at the top of this file.

  kvivo_max (https://github.com/dandanvidi/kvivo_max), the data of Davidi D,
  et al. Global characterization of in vivo enzyme catalytic rates and their
  correspondence to in vitro kcat measurements. PNAS 113:3401-3406 (2016).
  Copyright (c) 2015 dandanvidi

  small-molecule-regulation (https://github.com/eladnoor/small-molecule-regulation),
  whose metabolite concentrations are those of Gerosa L, et al. Pseudo-transition
  analysis identifies the key regulators of dynamic metabolic adaptations from
  steady-state data. Cell Systems 1:270-282 (2015).
  Copyright (c) 2016 Elad Noor
